in @optics/source

# @optics/source/ganglion — the per-ganglion gain media sub-family.
#
# Sub-prism under @optics/source declaring the 5 gain media that
# correspond to Fate's connectome ganglia. Per docs/specs/optical-
# keywords.md §10.3, Fate's connectome IS a five-layer diffractive
# deep neural network (Lin et al. 2018, Science 361:1004-1008): each
# ganglion is a 90-port diffractive surface; the 5 ganglia chained
# in series form the D²NN; the produced eigenmode IS the tournament
# verdict.
#
# Per §10.2 (the kintsugi loop IS a resonator with output coupler),
# the ACTIVE pass of the kintsugi loop requires gain to drive each
# ganglion's transit toward convergence. Without per-ganglion gain
# media, the cavity-enhanced spectrograph reading (§12.3,
# DOAS-with-feedback per Brown 2003) cannot close.
#
# === Species under this sub-family ===
#
# One source per ganglion in `boot/std/fate/connectome.mirror`:
#
#   @optics/source/ganglion/abyss         the depth-reading ganglion
#                                          (recursive inward gaze).
#   @optics/source/ganglion/introject     the pattern-recognition
#                                          ganglion (internalised
#                                          structures).
#   @optics/source/ganglion/cartographer  the mapping ganglion
#                                          (terrain charting).
#   @optics/source/ganglion/explorer      the exploratory ganglion
#                                          (under-tried territory).
#   @optics/source/ganglion/fate          the selector ganglion
#                                          (final tournament arbiter).
#
# === Why v1 lands all 5 with uniform shape ===
#
# Per docs/specs/optical-keywords.md §10.5, the tournament's rule
# composition (`tabu(t)`, `ucb(c)`, etc.) maps to multi-mode pumping
# discipline — each ganglion's gain profile would, in principle,
# specialize per its tournament-rule preferences. v1 declares all 5
# with uniform shape (formalism: s_matrix for 90×90 D²NN topology;
# action: refract for phase-only diffractive transit; pumping: io;
# gain_curve / saturation: ref discharged at @io). Per-ganglion
# specialization (different gain curve shapes, different saturation
# envelopes) lands when the cascade pulls the second-instance
# substrate-pull-realize candidate that surfaces from the energy-
# balance opacity map at runtime.
#
# === The substrate-pull on `keyword_matches_depth` ===
#
# Per docs/specs/optical-keywords.md §1, `source` is a NEW top-level
# declaration keyword (alongside facet / stage / aperture / splitter
# / resonator / bench / detector). The current
# `@epistemologic/pact/keyword_matches_depth` predicate enumerates
# `prism | glass | pact` only; it does NOT yet recognize `source`.
# This shard's first operational use of `source` at depth 3
# generates the opacity that drives the property's substrate-pull —
# the next tick lifts `declared_keywords`'s domain to include the
# spec §1 NEW keywords. Substrate-pull discipline: declare what the
# spec defines; let the opacity surface; let the next tick close it.
#
# Per [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]]: `glass
# @optics/source/ganglion { ... }` declares this IS a sub-prism of
# @optics/source.
#
# Spec context: docs/specs/optical-keywords.md §1.7 (source keyword),
#               §3.9 (source_declares_energy_balance property),
#               §10.1 (Fate's optical mapping; the five ganglia as
#               splitter layers); §10.3 (D²NN identification);
#               §10.8 (Surface B: the gain-medium gap this tick
#               closes).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-alignment-as-boundary-mathematics]]
#                      (recognition #57; the @io boundary crossing
#                      that ganglion pumping carries).
# Related shards: boot/std/fate/connectome.mirror (the ganglion type;
#                 `type ganglion = abyss | introject | cartographer
#                 | explorer | fate`; this sub-family declares one
#                 source per variant),
#                 boot/std/fate/tournament.mirror (the tournament
#                 rules whose pumping discipline each gain medium
#                 carries),
#                 kintsugi/oscillate.mirror (the resonator whose
#                 ACTIVE pass these gain media drive).
# Path-namespace property: this file at
# `shards/optics/source/ganglion.mirror` declares
# `@optics/source/ganglion` as the sub-family root; species live at
# `shards/optics/source/ganglion/<name>.mirror`.

glass @optics/source/ganglion {
  focus ganglion
  project ganglion
  split ganglion
  shift ganglion
  settle ganglion
}

out @optics/source/ganglion
